# Keeps the Docker build context — and with it the CDK asset hash — a function of the agent's own
# sources.
#
# CDK's DockerImageAsset fingerprints and stages only what survives this file. Without it the
# context is the whole package (node_modules included), so any `npm install` changes the hash and
# forces a full image rebuild and push even when no agent source changed.

# Installed inside the image by `npm ci`. Copying the host tree in would also drag the host's
# architecture into an arm64 image, on top of being reinstalled anyway.
node_modules

# Produced by `npm run build` inside the image.
dist

# Runtime configuration comes from the AgentCore runtime environment, never from a file in the image.
.env
.env.*

# Not needed to build or run the agent.
**/__tests__
*.test.ts
README.md
